            <span class="text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3 font-medium">
            In combustion engines, efficiency is measured in distance per unit of liquid fuel (km per liter or MPG). In electric vehicles, energy is measured in kilowatt-hours (kWh), equivalent to 1 unit of electricity on your domestic utility meter. A rating of 30 km/kWh means the vehicle travels 30 kilometers using 1 unit of electric energy.
          </p>
